  "full": {
   "text": "<<effects of social media on mental health of teenagers>>  \n\nplatforms play a significant role in shaping the mental health of teenagers through constant exposure to curated content and comparison with others. this exposure can lead to feelings of inadequacy and anxiety, especially when teenagers compare their lives to the idealized versions presented on social media. the impact of social media on mental health is complex and varies depending on factors such as usage patterns, content type, and individual differences.  \n\nresearch findings indicate a correlation between high levels of social media use and lower self-esteem, increased anxiety, and decreased sleep quality among teenagers. the study suggests that while social media can connect individuals and provide support, it also poses risks that need to be addressed through education and awareness. the results highlight the importance of developing strategies to promote healthy social media use and support mental well-being.",
